From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:17:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] droidcamsrc: report the latency in nanoseconds

The LATENCY query answered 33 and 33 * 7 for the 7 buffers at 30 fps
that the comment above it assumes, but latencies are GstClockTime
nanoseconds: the source claimed 33 ns, not 33 ms. Report 33 ms and
231 ms, as meant.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c
index c5e7c23..609d142 100644
--- a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c
+++ b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c
@@ -1641,7 +1641,8 @@ gst_droidcamsrc_pad_query (GstPad * pad, GstObject * parent, GstQuery * query)
 
     case GST_QUERY_LATENCY:
       /* TODO: this assummes 7 buffers @ 30 FPS. Query from either bufferpool or camera params */
-      gst_query_set_latency (query, TRUE, 33, 33 * 7);
+      gst_query_set_latency (query, TRUE, 33 * GST_MSECOND,
+          33 * 7 * GST_MSECOND);
       ret = TRUE;
       break;
 
